      "content": "It's important to stay calm. Feeling monitored or experiencing increased pressure can be common, especially in high-stakes work environments. However, obsessing over every little action might not be healthy or necessary. Focus on maintaining efficiency, being punctual, and adhering to company policies. Furthermore, practicing mindfulness, taking breaks, and maintaining a work-life balance can help reduce stress. Remember, it's natural to make mistakes. Letting small errors roll off you won't affect the big picture of your professional growth and reliability. If you feel these feelings are overwhelming, consider discussing it with HR or a manager to address any underlying issues directly.",
